cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Measuring the Wealth of Nations: Replication Package"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both this replication package and the original Shaikh & Tonak (1994) work."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nick
    email: protonnicky@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/measuring-wealth-of-nations-replication"
abstract: >-
  Complete replication and extension of every empirical claim in Shaikh & Tonak's
  Measuring the Wealth of Nations (1994), plus 8 follow-up studies (Tonak 1984,
  Shaikh & Tonak 1987 and 2002, Moos 2017, Mohun 2005 and 2013, Karabacak & Tonak
  2022 Turkey, Cronin 2001 New Zealand), with 64 data series covering 1925-2025.
  Built on the Anu Framework v10.0 with strict no-fabrication and full-provenance
  discipline; every value traces to a published source, cached API response, or
  documented derivation. 100% validation pass rate against book benchmarks and
  identity/cross-source consistency checks.
keywords:
  - marxian-economics
  - replication
  - shaikh-tonak
  - net-social-wage
  - rate-of-exploitation
  - input-output
  - heterodox-economics
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-15"
references:
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Shaikh
        given-names: Anwar
      - family-names: Tonak
        given-names: E. Ahmet
    title: "Measuring the Wealth of Nations: The Political Economy of National Accounts"
    publisher: Cambridge University Press
    year: 1994
    isbn: "9780521564793"
